    "finalPromptText": "I'm working on a final paper for my sci-fi literature course and I'm considering writing about Project Hail Mary by Andy Weir. Can you help me find some background on the book — when it came out, what it's about, and how it was received critically?",
    "finalAssistantVisibleText": "**Project Hail Mary** by Andy Weir is a science fiction novel released in **2021**. The story follows Ryland Grace, a middle-school science teacher who awakens from a coma aboard a spacecraft with no memory of how he got there. He gradually pieces together that he is humanity's last hope sent on a desperate one-way mission to combat an organism called Astrophage, which is threatening to dim the Sun and endanger life on Earth. The narrative alternates between present events aboard the ship and flashbacks to mission planning on Earth. \n\nKey themes of the novel include:\n- Science and problem-solving\n- First contact\n- Sacrifice\n- Friendship\n- Survival\n\nThe book has approximately **117,000 words** and has been well-received critically. It has been praised for its optimistic tone, scientific rigor, and character development, particularly the heartwarming relationship between Grace and an alien named Rocky. Reviewers often compare it to Weir's previous work, *The Martian*, as well as to *Rendezvous with Rama*.\n\n### Critical Reception\n1. It has high ratings, averaging **4.8/5** based on over **47,812 ratings**, making it one of the highest-rated recent science fiction novels.\n2. Many publications named it one of the best science fiction novels of 2021.\n3. The optimistic outlook and engaging protagonist have received particular acclaim.\n\nFor more detailed information, including a comprehensive summary, you can visit its [Wikipedia page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Hail_Mary).\n\nIf you need further insights or specific aspects about the book, feel free to ask!",
